 "notes": [
  "Default band D2 has no frames at all in partial visits v2 (D1/D4 only) and v4 (D3/D6 only), so those visits have no D2 co-add. v6 D2 is a single frame. Every other target has its default band in every visit.",
  "Frames: 351 used of 358 fetched; rejected {'wl_out_of_band': 7, 'offdetector': 0}. 1 frames had the target within 10.0 px of the strip/detector edge, so no forced photometry for them.",
  "Input coordinate (Gaia DR3 4472832130942575872 catalogue position at J2016.0 (the brief gives no coordinate)) is 105.6 arcsec (17.2 px) from the mean-epoch (2026-03-03) proper-motion-corrected position the grid is centred on.",
  "Saturated: 349 of 350 forced-photometry points have OVERFLOW/NONLINEAR pixels inside the aperture, so their flux is null and the binned spectrum is empty. This is the expected result for a K~4.5 star, not a pipeline failure.",
  "The co-add cores are masked (NaN in .f32, black in the PNG, white in the mask). Motion is measured with a 2D Gaussian fitted to the unmasked PSF wings (r<=5 px), see checks.motion_first_last_full_visit.",
  "Visits v2, v4 and v6 are partial (2-10 frames, some bands only). The default diff uses the full visits v1 (Aug-Sep 2025) and v5 (Aug-Sep 2026).",
  "Brief: the challenge gives no coordinate for this target. input.* is the Gaia DR3 catalogue position at J2016.0.",
  "Pixel data: SPHEREx Level-2 spectral images (spherex_dr1, plus spherex_qr3 where SIA returned them), read by HTTP range requests from s3://nasa-irsa-spherex (IMAGE and VARIANCE strips, row-tiled RICE FLAGS decompressed locally, WCS-WAVE table, EPSF row). One frame was checked byte-identical to the IRSA cutout service for IMAGE, FLAGS and VARIANCE.",
  "Frame filter: the wavelength at the target pixel comes from the 'W' WCS (WAVE-TAB, sip=None) and must lie inside the detector's em_min..em_max. Visits are clusters with no gap >20 days. A visit is 'full' when every band D1-D6 has >=5 frames.",
  "Co-adds: each frame has its sigma-clipped median subtracted (local zodi/background removal) and pixels with any of SUR_ERROR, TRANSIENT, OVERFLOW, NONLINEAR, NONFUNC, DICHROIC, MISSING_DATA, HOT, COLD, PHANMISS, PERSIST, OUTLIER, CROSSTALK, GHOST, GHOST_FPA, GHOST_EXT, STREAK, BLOOM, SNOWBALL or HALO masked. Frames are bilinearly resampled (normalised by the good-pixel weight, needing weight >=0.5) through the full SIP WCS onto the common grid, then median-combined per visit per band."
 ],
